+# PHASE 5.0J-2-RG03 — Repository-owner run instructions
+
+Status: CI PREPARED, NOT EXECUTED. This package is verification infrastructure, not a Release Candidate. No deployment is configured.
+
+## 1. Use an authorized isolated verification repository
+
+The supplied runner package contains the unchanged `qalba-platform/` application, the exact authorized RG03 MIME harness, the two original input archives, the authoritative manifest, and CI-only files.
+
+Extract the contents of `Quddam-Phase-5.0J-2-GHA-Verification-Runner.zip` into the root of a dedicated private verification repository. Keep `.github/` and `.gitignore`, including when your file browser hides them. Do not overlay a different application checkout, merge missing source from another phase, or flatten `qalba-platform/`.
+
+At repository root these paths must exist:
+
+| Path | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `.github/workflows/quddam-rg03-release-verification.yml` | Manual-only three-job workflow |
+| `.github/actions/rg03-runtime/action.yml` | Shared provisioning/readiness procedure |
+| `ci/` | Integrity, CI adapters, orchestration, accounting, safe packaging |
+| `qalba-platform/` | Exact 670-file frozen RG02 application |
+| `verification-tools/` | Exact authorized 22-file RG03 harness |
+| `inputs/Quddam-Phase-5.0J-2-RG02-frozen-checkpoint.zip` | Original baseline; latest safe checkpoint |
+| `inputs/Quddam-Phase-5.0J-2-RG03-Evidence.zip` | Original authorized MIME correction/provenance |
+| `Source-Manifest.json` | Authoritative application file hashes |
+| `CI-Source-Manifest.json` | Exact prepared CI file hashes |
+| `Quddam-Phase-5.0J-2-Test-Manifest.json` | All 447 mandatory identities, initially NOT_EXECUTED |
+
+The repository owner, using their own authorization, must make the files available on the repository's default branch. This preparation session has not initialized a Git repository, committed, pushed, opened a PR, configured credentials or dispatched a workflow. Publishing these verification files is the owner's separate action; no product-repository change is needed.
+
+Before uploading, an owner with Python 3 can run the read-only integrity check from the extracted package root:
+
+```bash
+python3 ci/baseline.py verify
+```
+
+Do not add a production `.env`, database URL, SMTP credentials, payment keys or customer data. No repository secrets are required by this workflow. The service uses explicitly test-only credentials; auth/cron/callback secrets are generated by the preserved verification runners. Payment tests use the existing local synthetic provider contracts, not real-money operations.
+
+Enable GitHub Actions and allow the pinned official `actions/*` actions. Use GitHub.com Ubuntu-hosted runners, not GitHub Enterprise Server artifact backends or an unreviewed self-hosted machine. The repository account must have enough Actions minutes/storage for a potentially multi-hour gate. Each job has a fresh isolated PostgreSQL service and independently re-proves readiness.
+
+## 2. Start ONE fresh workflow
+
+In the repository, open **Actions → Quddam PHASE 5.0J-2-RG03 Release Verification → Run workflow**. Select the default branch containing the exact package and click **Run workflow** once.
+
+Alternatively, from an already-authorized owner session in that repository:
+
+```bash
+gh workflow run quddam-rg03-release-verification.yml --ref main
+gh run watch
+```
+
+Replace `main` only if the repository has a different default branch. Do not use an older source ref. No command above was executed by this preparation session.
+
+Manual workflow dispatch requires the workflow to exist on the default branch and the operator to have repository write access. See the [official GitHub manual-run instructions](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/manage-workflow-runs/manually-run-a-workflow).
+
+## 3. What must happen, in order
+
+| Job / stage | Mandatory prerequisite and behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `runtime-readiness` | Exact input hashes; Node 24.19.0; `npm ci`; signed native PG16 packages; official locked Playwright Chromium; real PG16 connection and all 24 migrations; native startup/locking/immediate-stop/restart/dump/restore/shutdown smoke; browser launch; unchanged app/harness/CI hashes |
+| `targeted-m05` preparation | Independently re-prove readiness on the new host; generate route types and prepare a clean production build, with frozen generated declaration bytes restored |
+| First targeted identity | Unchanged canonical M05 reset-mail scenario, 60-second canonical timeout, original assertions, exact authorized MIME decoding |
+| Related targeted identities | Five other public-ingress M05 auth/abuse identities and five H01 Host-session revocation identities, including password-reset revocation; 10 total |
+| RG03 freeze | Only after 1/1 M05 and 10/10 related PASS, zero retries/skips; application/harness/CI/combined fingerprints and runtime receipt included |
+| `complete-final-gate` | New host, fresh readiness; verify the checkpoint from this same run/SHA; fresh full quality/unit/content/operations gates; native identity 001; canonical identity 001; M13 and all supplemental groups; independent exact-count audit |
+| Final packaging | Release Candidate and five required final deliverables ONLY after 223 + 38 + 186 and 1185 unit/integration, all quality gates, zero failures/skips/retries/flaky |
+
+Browser CLI uses `--max-failures=1 --retries=0`, one worker. Vitest uses one file worker with bail 1 and retry 0. No assertion or timeout was increased. A failed step prevents later mandatory jobs/stages; only evidence export/upload runs after failure.
+
+The original native main suites execute 163 identities; M13 adds 23, totaling 186. Existing M13/launch flags suppress redundant copies of already-covered native suites, not mandatory identities. Supplemental content/launch setup may re-exercise passed native fixture logic in fresh databases; those extra fixture checks never inflate the 186 unique identity count.
+
+PostgreSQL service container is not used to impersonate M13. Native runners execute real runner-owned PostgreSQL 16 binaries in disposable loopback-only clusters with their original lifecycle control and fixture assertions.
+
+## 4. Preserve the first failure and STOP
+
+Do not click **Re-run jobs**, retry a failed identity, change a timeout, weaken an assertion, skip a test, or patch product/canonical tests. Workflow attempts above 1 are refused so they cannot replace the original run evidence. Diagnose the preserved failure under a separate explicit authorization before any further attempt.
+
+If an installation, migration, launch, source guard or mandatory identity fails, the workflow stops. Cause remains **D — UNRESOLVED** until the original evidence proves A product defect, B harness defect or C CI/environment failure. A native source callback/stack is used for exact identity attribution where available; errors outside a case retain the exact source/task and are not mislabeled as a product identity failure.
+
+If GitHub's platform fails before checkout or job startup, use its native job/platform error log; custom receipts cannot exist before repository code executes. If the hosted job reaches GitHub's six-hour limit, that is an incomplete gate, never a PASS; do not resume counts from it. Do not introduce automatic reruns/sharding to claim completion.
+
+## 5. Download artifacts promptly
+
+Artifacts are kept for 14 days:
+
+| Artifact name | Contents |
+| --- | --- |
+| `rg03-readiness-RUN_ID` | Runtime/source receipts; safe prerequisite errors if any |
+| `rg03-targeted-RUN_ID` | Actual M05/related results; first failure evidence OR newly frozen RG03 checkpoint |
+| `rg03-final-RUN_ID` | Fresh manifest/counts, safe logs/diagnostic trace, source/runtime receipts, latest safe checkpoint, blocked report OR complete release deliverables |
+
+Shared evidence is intentionally allowlisted and redacted. Raw browser traces, cookies, request bodies, DOM snapshots, screenshots/QR resources, SMTP messages, private fixtures, database dumps, TLS keys and generated credentials are not uploaded. The safe trace is a diagnostic event stream, not a replayable raw Playwright trace. Original private-file hashes preserve provenance without publishing their contents.
+
+An artifact's existence is not a release PASS. Accept only the actual final report stating **READY FOR RELEASE VERIFICATION**, accompanied by the independent manifest showing 223/223 canonical, 38/38 supplemental, 186/186 native, 1185/1185 unit/integration, all required quality gates, zero failed/skipped/retries/flaky.
+
+If blocked, preserve the first-failure run URL, safe evidence ZIP, report, exact source fingerprints and latest safe checkpoint. RG02 remains latest safe until targeted M05 and related tests actually produce an RG03 freeze.
+
+## 6. Hard stop
+
+This workflow does not deploy, use production databases, perform real-money transactions, enforce CSP, add features, redesign Quddam, commit/push, create releases, or begin another phase. CSP remains `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only`.
+
+Stop after the actual complete PASS or first blocker. Return the run URL and artifacts for review; do not perform a production deployment from this verification workflow.
